  "_note": "S29/C140. The SAME harness, run twice: `control` resets both root nodes to the spawn transforms at every beat (C138's shipped behaviour, and it reproduces C138's published joins to the digit); `chain` carries the previous beat's live root transforms forward instead. The joins do not move, so the reset was never the cause. `_align_pair` best-fits a rigid transform over 360 yaw candidates and measures the residual AFTER applying it, so the base transform is washed out and the residual is a POSE mismatch no rotation or translation can remove."
